sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant App as Caller
    participant C as Cache (map + list)
    participant W as WAL
    participant S as Snapshot
    App->>C: get(key)
    C->>C: move node to head — a read mutates state
    Note over C,W: recency order is deliberately not durable
    C-->>App: value (no disk write)
    App->>C: put(key, value)
    C->>W: append {seq, PUT, key, value, crc}
    Note over W: fsync policy is the durability guarantee
    C-->>App: ack after the buffered append
    S->>S: periodic snapshot in LRU order, atomic rename
    S->>W: truncate below the snapshot seq
    Note over C,S: recovery = newest valid snapshot + WAL tail, stop at the first bad CRC
